{"position":336,"sourceId":"ui.romarr-recognizes-platform-slugs-and.dbdab9544b","source":"ROMarr recognizes platform slugs and unambiguous ES-DE system names automatically. Add a mapping only when your existing folder uses another name, such as","sourceSha256":"dbdab9544be1d0904c54fb778fcf432ac4aef859064e4083908466a06f99aae2","sourceKind":null,"reportedLocations":["romarr/ui.py:3922"],"productionCallerCount":1,"localizableUiMessageEstablished":true,"callerContextRefs":[{"path":"romarr/ui.py","lineStart":4186,"lineEnd":4190,"contextLines":[{"line":4186,"text":"  +`<div class=\"help\" style=\"margin:-6px 0 14px\">Use one ROM root with one folder per platform, such as <code>Emulation/roms/ps2</code> and <code>Emulation/roms/snes</code>; you do not need a separate library entry for each system. With EmuDeck, point this at its <code>Emulation/roms</code> folder, not the wider <code>Emulation</code> directory. Keep shared metadata alongside it at <code>Emulation/metadata</code>${interfaceMarkup(', outside the ROM root, and mount that folder on each client. ROMarr keeps one catalog per platform and deduplicated artwork here, so a rename or path change does not trigger another provider lookup.')}</div>`"},{"line":4187,"text":"  +`<fieldset class=\"settings-group\"><legend>Platform folder names</legend>"},{"line":4188,"text":"    <p class=\"help\" style=\"margin:4px 0 8px\">ROMarr recognizes platform slugs and unambiguous ES-DE system names automatically. Add a mapping only when your existing folder uses another name, such as <code>PS2 Games</code>. Folder names are matched only at the library root.</p>"},{"line":4189,"text":"    <div id=\"platform-folder-mappings\">${platformFolderRows(SETTINGS.platform_folder_mappings)}</div>"},{"line":4190,"text":"    <button class=\"btn ghost\" id=\"platform-folder-mapping-add\" type=\"button\">Add folder mapping</button></fieldset>`"}],"contextSha256":"3242582e0e6105019f1324044cf0b11b6af15567a9fb383fe5217ece3675ffb7","fileSha256":"732486b957967ecde0457be53f8f70bf6675df5c9d7d340bb2c2d963bb23661a","gitBlob":"a99731cc16d32a6e7385108d07de057097bda722"}],"callerResolutionHold":false,"callerResolutionRationale":"Current source context is pinned below; the message is visibly used in the UI or a UI response."}
{"position":337,"sourceId":"ui.romarr-reports-what-it-can-verify-ab.7a47672fa2","source":"ROMarr reports what it can verify about one and never guesses the rest.","sourceSha256":"7a47672fa293008f2205d1dbbfc9067f55cbb3177c7d428f34ac85897b6d8592","sourceKind":null,"reportedLocations":["romarr/ui.py:4523"],"productionCallerCount":1,"localizableUiMessageEstablished":true,"callerContextRefs":[{"path":"romarr/ui.py","lineStart":4784,"lineEnd":4789,"contextLines":[{"line":4784,"text":"    <p class=\"help\">${m.hint?apiMessageMarkup(m.hint):''}. A Moonlight host renders a real"},{"line":4785,"text":"    desktop emulator on the host's GPU and sends video &mdash; which is how"},{"line":4786,"text":"    machines with no browser core get played. ROMarr reports what it can"},{"line":4787,"text":"    verify about one and never guesses the rest.</p>"},{"line":4788,"text":"    <p class=\"help\">${apiMessageMarkup(m.manual||'')}</p></div>`;"},{"line":4789,"text":""}],"contextSha256":"dba85cf6e2ff72ef6af12c57f7dc9aca255dd84d73e8b91676571d8b70d0bf8e","fileSha256":"732486b957967ecde0457be53f8f70bf6675df5c9d7d340bb2c2d963bb23661a","gitBlob":"a99731cc16d32a6e7385108d07de057097bda722"}],"callerResolutionHold":false,"callerResolutionRationale":"Current source context is pinned below; the message is visibly used in the UI or a UI response."}
